-- HTMLRules universal --
In documents read as HTML, a processing instruction ends at the first ">",
like the bogus comment HTML parsers read, and is a bogus comment unless that
">" follows "?", as in HTML mode with XML syntax. After an XML declaration,
the ones before the first tag end at "?>", as in XML mode.
-- in --
<?xml version="1.0"?><?xml-stylesheet href="a>b.css"?><?pi a>b?><p>Hello<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:o" /><o:p></o:p></p><p><?php echo $a->b; ?><?pi x?><?><??></p><x:y xmlns:x="urn:x"><?pi a>b?></x:y><p><?php echo
-- tokens --
0 ProcInst xml "<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>" data=" version=\"1.0\""
0 ProcInst xml-stylesheet "<?xml-stylesheet href=\"a>b.css\"?>" data=" href=\"a>b.css\""
0 ProcInst pi "<?pi a>b?>" data=" a>b"
1 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
1 Text "Hello" text="Hello"
1 Comment [bogus] "<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = \"urn:o\" />" text="?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = \"urn:o\" /"
2 StartTag o:p "<o:p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
2 EndTag o:p "</o:p>"
1 EndTag p "</p>"
1 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
1 Comment [bogus] "<?php echo $a->" text="?php echo $a-"
1 Text "b; ?>" text="b; ?>"
1 ProcInst pi "<?pi x?>" data=" x"
1 Comment [bogus] "<?>" text="?"
1 ProcInst  "<??>" data=""
1 EndTag p "</p>"
1 StartTag x:y "<x:y xmlns:x=\"urn:x\">" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:x="urn:x"
1 Comment [bogus] "<?pi a>" text="?pi a"
1 Text "b?>" text="b?>"
1 EndTag x:y "</x:y>"
1 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
1 Comment [incomplete] [bogus] [unsound] "<?php echo" text="?php echo"
1 EndTag p [implied] ""
-- HTMLRulesProlog universal --
Without an XML declaration, the ones before the first tag also end at the
first ">".
-- in --
<?xml-stylesheet href="a>b.css"?><?pi a?><p>x</p>
-- tokens --
0 Comment [bogus] "<?xml-stylesheet href=\"a>" text="?xml-stylesheet href=\"a"
0 Text "b.css\"?>" text="b.css\"?>"
0 ProcInst pi "<?pi a?>" data=" a"
1 StartTag p "<p>" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
1 Text "x" text="x"
1 EndTag p "</p>"
-- PrologUnterminated universal --
After an XML declaration, one before the first tag without "?>" up to the end
of the input ends at the first ">" after all, as a bogus comment, and an
incomplete bogus comment without a ">".
-- in --
<?xml version="1.0"?><?a><?b x>
<?c
-- tokens --
0 ProcInst xml "<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>" data=" version=\"1.0\""
0 Comment [bogus] "<?a>" text="?a"
0 Comment [bogus] "<?b x>" text="?b x"
0 Text "\n" text="\n"
0 Comment [incomplete] [bogus] [unsound] "<?c" text="?c"
-- XHTML universal --
In documents following XML rules, processing instructions end at "?>".
-- in --
<?xml version="1.0"?><?pi a>b?><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><?pi a>b?></html><?pi a>b?>
-- tokens --
0 ProcInst xml "<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>" data=" version=\"1.0\""
0 ProcInst pi "<?pi a>b?>" data=" a>b"
1 StartTag html "<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">" ns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
1 ProcInst pi "<?pi a>b?>" data=" a>b"
1 EndTag html "</html>"
0 ProcInst pi "<?pi a>b?>" data=" a>b"
